<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnus Olafsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1265">1265</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Magnus, King of Mann and the Isles</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnus Olafsson was the last king of Mann and the Isles of the Crovan dynasty, reigning from 1254 to 1265. He supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-iv-of-norway">Haakon IV of Norway</a> in the campaign that ended at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-largs">Battle of Largs</a> in 1263, then submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-scotland">Alexander III of Scotland</a>. After his death, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> ceded Man and the Isles to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a> in 1266.</p></div>
